  {
   "title": "Initial Impressions from the LSU game",
   "link": "https://www.rollbamaroll.com/alabama-crimson-tide-football/86232/alabama-football-initial-impressions-from-the-lsu-game",
   "source": "Roll Bama Roll",
   "summary": "Alabama and LSU faced off yesterday, in a battle of two-loss SEC foes fighting for their playoff lives. The Tigers were ranked outside the playoff field and were thus the more desperate team. Unfortunately for them, they hired Lane Kiffin who tends to make very questionable decisions in desperate moments. Lane called for a first [&#8230;]",
   "image": "https://platform.rollbamaroll.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/138/2026/11/gettyimages-2304045331.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0,0,100,100",
   "sourceLogo": null,
   "published": "2026-11-08T14:25:08+00:00"
  },
  {
   "title": "No. 5/9/9 Alabama Rolls Past No. 14/15/15 LSU, 31-13, in Baton Rouge",
   "link": "https://rolltide.com/news/2026/11/7/football-no-5-9-9-alabama-rolls-past-no-14-15-15-lsu-31-13-in-baton-rouge",
   "source": "Alabama Athletics",
   "summary": "<img alt=\"Yhonzae Pierre Tackle at LSU\" src=\"https://rolltide.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/7/Yhonzae_Pierre_Tackle_at_LSU.jpg\" /><br /><br />BATON ROUGE, La. - No. 5/9/9 Alabama football (7-2, 5-2 SEC) picked up its second ranked road victory of the season, taking down No. 14/15/15 LSU (6-3, 3-3 SEC), 31-13, inside Tiger Stadium. The Crimson Tide scored the final 21 points in the contest within a 9:13 span over the third and fourth quarters to secure the win.",
   "image": "https://rolltide.com/images/2026/11/7/Yhonzae_Pierre_Tackle_at_LSU.jpg?width=800",
   "sourceLogo": "https://rolltide.com/favicon.ico",
   "published": "2026-11-08T01:50:00+00:00"
  },
  {
   "title": "Victory/Late Shift Open Thread: Alabama tames Tigers once again",
   "link": "https://www.rollbamaroll.com/alabama-crimson-tide-football/86218/alabama-football-lsu-open-thread-alabama-tames-tigers-once-again",
   "source": "Roll Bama Roll",
   "summary": "Alabama rolled into Baton Rouge with a chorus of voices across the sport telling them how overrated they are. They came away with a blowout on the road to silence each and every one of them, beating LSU 31-13. Based on the first drive for both teams, it looked like LSU was clearly the better [&#8230;]",
   "image": "https://platform.rollbamaroll.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/138/2026/11/reuters-tagreuters.com2026newsml_MT1USATODAY303023081955458151.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0,0,100,100",
   "sourceLogo": null,
   "published": "2026-11-08T00:22:23+00:00"
  },
  {
   "title": "Alabama vs LSU: First Half Impressions",
   "link": "https://www.rollbamaroll.com/alabama-crimson-tide-football/86213/alabama-vs-lsu-first-half-impressions",
   "source": "Roll Bama Roll",
   "summary": "On a play to play basis, LSU felt like a better team than the Tide through most of the first half. They moved the ball with consistency on nearly every drive, while the Alabama offense had a few stutters and gave up their share of negative plays. And yet, the Tide enters halftime with a [&#8230;]",
   "image": "https://platform.rollbamaroll.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/138/2026/11/gettyimages-2304009353.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0,0,100,100",
   "sourceLogo": null,
   "published": "2026-11-07T22:27:01+00:00"
  },
  {
   "title": "Wake Up! Week 10 Viewing Guide and Morning Open Thread",
   "link": "https://www.rollbamaroll.com/alabama-crimson-tide-football/86191/wake-up-week-10-viewing-guide-and-morning-open-thread",
   "source": "Roll Bama Roll",
